<title>LITHUANIA: Yields fall at sale of Lithuania 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yields fall at sale of Lithuania 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield at an auction of 91-day Lithuanian Treasury bills fell on Monday and demand exceeded supply as the issue was over-subscribed, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV YIELD   LAST TIME   MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID  SOLD</p>
<p>  91-day     8.22	 9.04	8.20/8.24   30  115.327 30</p>
<p>The settlement date for today's auction was August 7 and the bills mature on November 6.</p>
<p>The next auction is on August 5, when 30 million litas of 182-day paper will be offered.</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom +370 2 223 517</p>
</text>
